    {
      "id": "a1-u02-d02-t01",
      "before": "a1-u02-d02-e01",
      "title": { "en": "On, ona, ono" },
      "body": { "en": "*On* is \"he\" and *ona* is \"she\". There is also *ono*, \"it\", for a child or a neuter thing. All three take *jest*. *To jest…* means \"this is…\" and introduces a person or a thing: *to jest Adam*." },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "być",
        "meaning": { "en": "to be" },
        "forms": { "ja": "jestem", "ty": "jesteś", "on": "jest", "my": "jesteśmy", "wy": "jesteście", "oni": "są" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u02-d02-t02",
      "before": "a1-u02-d02-e08",
      "title": { "en": "Where from" },
      "body": { "en": "*Skąd* asks \"where from\", and the answer is *z* with the country: *z Polski*, *z Anglii*. The country's ending changes after *z*, so for now learn yours as a whole: *z Irlandii*, *z Kanady*, *z Australii*, *z Brazylii*, *z Niemiec* (from Germany), *z USA*, *ze Szkocji* (from Scotland: *z* becomes *ze* before some groups of consonants)." }
    }
  ],
